      "location": "Definition",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "It says, “Equivalently, A=(LD)U is a normalised LU factorisation.” But def-normalised-lu-factorisation defines normalised LU by requiring its left factor to have every diagonal entry equal to 1. In an LDU factorisation diag(LD)=diag(D), which need not be 1; the scoped example uses D=diag(2,3). The normalised LU regrouping is A=L(DU), not (LD)U.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "b97096c85e8c680e4fc9537dca1d4b7eee85b50f9f30690867ab448170f9965b"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:3:2",
